  "sourceType": "SYNTHESISED",
  "sourceNotes": "This recipe synthesises the Iranian tradition of fragrant baked cakes (cake khak shir or keyk gerdui) scented with rose water and cardamom, as documented in Iranian cookery references including Najmieh Batmanglij's Food of Life (1986) and Maryam Sinaiee's The Saffron Tales (2016), with the Western yoghurt cake format. The use of full-fat yoghurt as the primary moistening agent, cardamom as the primary spice, and rose water as a secondary flavouring reflects the documented Iranian baking tradition.",
