  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Persian yoghurt cake is made by whisking wet and dry ingredients together in two bowls and combining them. The yoghurt keeps the crumb moist and the cardamom gives it a clean, floral warmth. Rose water is a balancing ingredient: use the full 2 tablespoons and the flavour reads as fragrant rather than perfumed. Use food-grade rose water; some cosmetic rose waters are too concentrated and bitter."
          }
        ]
      },
