      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the batter"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 170°C (conventional). Grease and line a 900 g loaf tin. Whisk {{caster-sugar}}, {{vegetable-oil}}, and {{eggs}} together in a large bowl until pale and slightly thickened. Whisk in {{greek-yoghurt}} and {{rose-water}}. Sift in {{plain-flour}}, {{cardamom-ground}}, {{baking-powder}}, {{bicarbonate-of-soda}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}}. Fold until just combined."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pour the batter into the tin and scatter {{pistachios}} over the surface. Bake for 45 to 50 minutes until a skewer inserted into the centre comes out clean and the top is deep golden. If the pistachios are browning too quickly, cover loosely with foil after 30 minutes. Leave in the tin for 20 minutes before turning out onto a wire rack. Serve at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
